  "question": {
    "text": "A heavy iron bar, of weight $W$ is having its one end on the ground and the other on the shoulder of a person. The bar makes an angle $\\theta$ with the horizontal. The weight experienced by the person is :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "Yji0c",
      "text": "$\\mathrm{W} \\cos \\theta$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "tZEC7",
      "text": "$\\frac{W}{2}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "qTITI",
      "text": "W",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "h59kM",
      "text": "$W \\sin \\theta$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/Lkw_0smKnZVjGSynS1By3yQPyBDFek91tyHOxlo-tso.original.fullsize.png\"><br />$R=$ net reaction force by shoulder\nBalancing torque about pt of contact on ground:\n$\\begin{aligned} & \\mathrm{W}\\left(\\frac{\\mathrm{L}}{2} \\cos \\theta\\right)=\\mathrm{R}(\\mathrm{L} \\cos \\theta) \\\\ & \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{R}=\\frac{\\mathrm{W}}{2}\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
